description:
Perform a Cyber Resilience Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/2847) Annex I essential-requirements review of RefDev, a networked RTEMS device: RTEMS 7 + rtems-lwip + shell, SPARC/LEON3. The device definition and its data-flow diagram are in the cra-review skill (`/workspace/.anvil/skills/cra-review/refdev.md`).

The checklist `/workspace/.anvil/skills/cra-review/annex1.yaml` is authoritative: assess every item as pass, gap, n/a or unknown, with cited evidence, and do not invent requirements. The checkout is the device's own firmware (lwIP stack, RTEMS port layer, GRETH driver, networking test application); assess the RTEMS kernel and shell as a third-party component.

Produce, in order:

1. gap analysis;
2. remediation plan: one Jira Story per gap in project RTEMS, labels `cra` and `tc3`, never `anvil`;
3. sandbox test evidence for 1-2 gaps;
4. a STRIDE threat model from the reference data-flow diagram;
5. a compliance report page in Confluence space RTKB;
6. SPDX and CycloneDX SBOMs.

A security engineer approves or rejects each gap; record rejections in `/memories/cra/lessons.md`.

Code base: branch `tc2/upgrade-base-leon3` of github.com/vishal7pandey/rtems-lwip.
